      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote",
        "text": "## Dither Studio - ordered vs error diffusion\n\nSame source, three bit-depth reducers:\n\n- **A - 1-bit mono, Atkinson** - error diffusion, like the classic Macintosh; spreads only 1/4 of the error to 4 of 8 neighbours, so contrast stays high.\n- **B - 3-level color, Bayer 8** - ordered dithering: fast, vectorised, regular crosshatch pattern.\n- **C - Game Boy palette, Floyd-Steinberg** - palette quantisation + full error diffusion through the CIELAB LUT.\n\nError-diffusion scans pixels sequentially - expect ~1 s per megapixel; ordered methods are ~50x faster."
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "## Dither Studio - ordered vs error diffusion\n\nSame source, three bit-depth reducers:\n\n- **A - 1-bit mono, Atkinson** - error diffusion, like the classic Macintosh; spreads only 1/4 of the error to 4 of 8 neighbours, so contrast stays high.\n- **B - 3-level color, Bayer 8** - ordered dithering: fast, vectorised, regular crosshatch pattern.\n- **C - Game Boy palette, Floyd-Steinberg** - palette quantisation + full error diffusion through the CIELAB LUT.\n\nError-diffusion scans pixels sequentially - expect ~1 s per megapixel; ordered methods are ~50x faster."
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
